    "q-213176": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213176",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14267734/assets/5f0776a65943d581b6e6fc93c3c09fa0c5c03a1a9b2feb5e092a1c23354f043e.png)\n\nThe plot of the binary relation $S,$ defined over the set $X=\\{♢,△,♡\\}$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(♡,♡)$\n\nII. $(△,♢)$\n\nIII. $(△,♡)$",
      "worked_solution": "A binary relation can be visualized using a plot (or graph), where \n\n- the first set is plotted along the horizontal axis,\n\n- the second set is plotted along the vertical axis, and\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines a point with coordinates $(x,y)$ on the plot.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given ordered pairs.\n\n- The pair $(♡,♡)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the plot contains a point with these coordinates.\n\n- The pair $(△,♢)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the plot contains a point with these coordinates.\n\n- The pair $(△,♡)$ does not belong to the relation since the plot does not contain a point with such coordinates.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
