    "q-213189": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213189",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Let $A=\\{-2,-1,0\\}$ and $B=\\{3,5,7\\}$ Which of the following is the graph representing the relation $R=\\{(x,y)\\in A\\times B\\,:\\,x+y\\le 3\\}?$",
      "worked_solution": "A binary relation can be visualized using a plot (or graph), where \n\n- the first set is plotted along the horizontal axis,\n\n- the second set is plotted along the vertical axis, and\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines a point with coordinates $(x,y)$ on the plot.\n\nThe relation $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in A\\times B$ with $x+y\\le 3.$\n\n- If $x=-2,$ then the values $y=3,5$ satisfy $x+y\\le 3.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(-2,3)$ and $(-2,5),$ and we should plot these points on the graph.\n\n- If $x=-1,$ then the value $y=3$ satisfies $x+y\\le 3.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(-1,3),$ and we should plot this point on the graph.\n\n- If $x=0,$ then the value $y=3$ satisfies $x+y\\le 3.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(0,3),$ and we should plot this point on the graph.\n\nTherefore, we have the following plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14267734/assets/f6a31765ddd4d82320767445e63bea7a727cce1349226a1ad0274ff129695931.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
