    "q-213177": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213177",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14267734/assets/223c0a0a36d0e1ae8e86943713ad55b26f5dfb33e21124c26903c9378e53ab5d.png)\n\nThe plot of the binary relation $S,$ defined over the set $X=\\{∅,\\{1\\},\\{2,3\\}\\}$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(∅,∅)$\n\nII. $(\\{2,3\\},\\{2,3\\})$\n\nIII. $(\\{2,3\\},\\{1\\})$",
      "worked_solution": "A binary relation can be visualized using a plot (or graph), where \n\n- the first set is plotted along the horizontal axis,\n\n- the second set is plotted along the vertical axis, and\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines a point with coordinates $(x,y)$ on the plot.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given ordered pairs.\n\n- The pair $(∅,∅)$ does not belong to the relation since the plot does not contain a point with such coordinates.\n\n- The pair $(\\{2,3\\},\\{2,3\\})$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the plot contains a point with these coordinates.\n\n- The pair $(\\{2,3\\},\\{1\\})$ does not belong to the relation since the plot does not contain a point with such coordinates.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
